# Commercial S7 credential-abort release refresh

- Observed at: 2026-08-30T10:46:00Z
- Scope: post-abort release binding
- Decision: keep S7 closed until the corrected release and fresh preflight pass

## Abort evidence

The reviewed S7 deployment reached service startup after green backup and
preflight. The runtime rejected the systemd 255 credential ACL, exited, and made
one bounded automatic retry. The Control abort path then proved:

- S7 service inactive/dead, disabled, `MainPID=0`;
- health timer disabled;
- port 8095 unbound;
- both pre-S7 Nginx files restored;
- application and Control worktrees clean;
- no provider, media, payment, or publishing activity.

## Corrected application release

Application PR #77 adds the exact root-managed systemd credential boundary
already used by Commercial S3 and retains strict local `0600` credentials.

- merge commit: `79a9d88d51ba5747cdfb0b6400a61506d82ccc6b`
- tree: `f3ae60f4c690a3b023db4e5953ca14050a9272b3`
- local tests: 786/786
- CI: Python 3.10/3.13 and PostgreSQL 17.11/18.6 green

## Control decision

Bind the S7 controller and manifest to the corrected application commit and
tree. All migration, contract, systemd-unit, health-script, and Nginx hashes
remain unchanged. A fresh backup verification and full preflight remain required
before any retry.

## Rollback

Revert this release-binding commit and leave the S7 service and health timer
disabled. The verified pre-deployment backup remains authoritative.
